  "faithful": "This is the most ponderous of all the known essential oils, but rises in distillation with sufficient ease: it appears limpid as water, has a moderately pungent taste, a very fragrant smell, exactly resembling that of the laffafras. It finds greatly commended as a fudorific, and for purifying the blood and juices: it is likewise supposed to be of service in humourous asthmas and coughs. The dose is from one drop to eight or ten, though Geoffroy goes as far as 20.",
